# Optional API keys for Sceneuron. Copy this file to .env and fill in only what you use.
#
# Every key is optional. Without any, Sceneuron still tracks presence and, on macOS, hand signals on
# the device, runs your rules and cards, and keeps the editor, the Stream Deck, hotkeys, and manual
# controls working. A key only turns on the cloud feature that needs it. A key saved in the
# editor's AI settings wins over one set here, and keys set here are never written to ai.json.
#
# Where Sceneuron reads this file:
# - The OBS plugin: .env in its config folder, for example
#   ~/Library/Application Support/obs-studio/plugin_config/sceneuron/.env on macOS, or the file
#   SCENEURON_ENV_FILE names.
# - sceneuron-dev --ai or --voice-wav: .env in the current folder, --env-file PATH, or the file
#   SCENEURON_ENV_FILE names, which wins over --env-file.
# Variables already set in the environment win over this file. Keep the file private
# (chmod 600 .env); Sceneuron warns when other users can read it.

# Gemini, for scene understanding, the assistant, and subtitle translations (AI settings provider
# "gemini", the default). Create a key in Google AI Studio for a project with the Gemini API:
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Keys created there since 2026-05-28 are auth keys, which
# Sceneuron sends the same way. Google refuses a key whose API restrictions do not allow the
# Generative Language API (the Gemini API), and the editor says so. Google also rejects
# unrestricted standard keys, so restrict an older key to the Generative Language API, or create
# one in AI Studio.
# Free tier (no billing): Google may use what is sent, camera images included, to improve its
# products, and people may review it. Keys from projects with billing are not used that way.
SCENEURON_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# An OpenAI-compatible endpoint such as NVIDIA NIM, for scene understanding, the assistant, and
# subtitle translations (AI settings provider "openai-compatible"). Local servers such as Ollama
# need no key.
SCENEURON_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# TypeSafe's Jev, for quick judgments of each condition from on-device facts. Only text facts
# are sent, never camera images, and only while scene understanding is on.
SCENEURON_JEV_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs, for voice control (speech to text) and spoken cards (text to speech). Microphone
# audio is sent only while voice control is on and you have consented, and in push-to-talk mode
# only while you hold the key; spoken cards send only the line to speak, and each line is
# generated once and cached.
SCENEURON_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
